### What's voice conversion?

Voice conversion lets you transform one person's voice into another’s. It uses a process called [voice cloning](https://elevenlabs.io/blog/what-is-voice-cloning) to encode the target voice - ie, the voice we convert to - and generate the same message spoken in a way which matches the target speaker’s identity but preserves the original intonation.

### Uses

High quality voice conversion and voice cloning technology have the potential to revolutionise the way content is produced, delivered and interacted with across a range of industries. They promise to optimise production time and costs and to provide those who share their voices to train conversion algorithms with ways to earn passive fees.

- In filmmaking actors could share their voice databases with producers to create audio tracks without the need to travel to set or studio;
- misspoken lines could be re-recorded much more effectively in post production;
- the technology can also be used to faithfully reproduce the voices of historical figures in fictional scenarios or to bring deceased actors back to life;
- video game development will find the technology useful to a similar extent: correcting utterances or simply experimenting could be done on the spot and without the actor physically present for recording;
- in medicine patients who lost the ability to speak, for example as a result of throat cancer treatment, can be given the chance to communicate again in their own voice;
